-- title:
--   Integrability of the S-part orbital-integral window at diag(u,1)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $\nu_{Z}$ a Haar measure on the idele units $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$, and $\xi$ a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top \le (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ whose associated $\mathbb{C}$-valued function is continuous. Fix a finite set $S$ of finite places, a unit $u \in K^\times$ with $u \neq 1$, an archimedean factor $f_\infty$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adele ring which is $\Phi \circ (\text{matrix entries in the mixed space})$ for some smooth $\Phi$ and has compact support, and for each finite place $v$ a function $f_v$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ that for $v \in S$ is locally constant with compact support. Write $\gamma_z = z\cdot I_2 \cdot \mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ for $z \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$, $u$ pushed into $\mathbb{A}_K$. Assume given: a constant $c_\tau>0$ and Haar measures $\tau_G(z)$ on the centraliser of $\gamma_z$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ whose integrals equal $c_\tau$ times the corresponding integral of $(x,y)\mapsto \mathrm{diag}(x,y)$ against $\nu_Z \times \nu_Z$; a Haar measure $\nu_A$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles; Haar measures $\tau_A(z)$ on the centraliser of the archimedean component of $\gamma_z$; Haar measures $\tau_F(z,v)$ on the centraliser of the $v$-component of $\gamma_z$, each giving mass $1$ to the integral set $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathcal{O}_v)$-locus; a constant $c_T>0$ together with the hypothesis that for all $z$, all finite $S'$, and all $W, W_\infty, (W_v)$ with the appropriate almost-everywhere strong measurability, with $W(t) = W_\infty(t_\infty)\prod_{v\in S'}W_v(t_v)$ whenever all components of $t$ outside $S'$ are integral and $W(t)=0$ otherwise, one has $\int W \,d\tau_G(z) = c_T(\int W_\infty \,d\tau_A(z))\prod_{v\in S'}\int W_v \,d\tau_F(z,v)$; a product-measure datum $P$ for $(S,\nu_Z)$ whose valuation function is the adelic order, whose projection is the $S$-part map, and whose measure $\nu_S$ satisfies $P.c \cdot \nu_S =$ the push-forward along the $S$-part map of $\nu_Z$ restricted to the ideles that are units outside $S$; and functions $I_\infty(z)$, $I_v(z)$ realising, for each $z$ and each $v \in S$, the orbital integral of $f_\infty$ at the archimedean component of $\gamma_z$ against $\nu_A$ and of $f_v$ at the $v$-component against the local Haar measure, each with respect to some section weight normalised by $\tau_A(z)$, respectively $\tau_F(z,v)$. Then the function $z_S \mapsto \xi(z_S)\bigl(I_\infty(z_S)\prod_{v\in S} I_v(z_S)\bigr)$ is integrable with respect to $\nu_S$.
--
--   This is the integrability statement needed to treat the $S$-part window of a product of local orbital integrals at the split regular class $\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$, $u \ne 1$, as an honest integral against the pinned $S$-part measure. It feeds the summation step in which such windows are compared with coefficient sums on the spectral side.
